@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Other SQL Server Data Types";
}

<section>

    <!-- =====================================================
         PAGE INTRODUCTION
         ===================================================== -->

    <div class="mb-5">

        <h1 class="fw-bold mb-3">
            Other SQL Server Data Types
        </h1>

        <p class="lead text-muted">
            SQL Server provides several other data types for storing
            Boolean values, monetary values, unique identifiers, binary
            data, XML documents and other specialized information.
        </p>

    </div>


    <!-- =====================================================
         WHAT ARE OTHER DATA TYPES?
         ===================================================== -->

    <section class="mb-5">

        <h3 class="fw-bold mb-3">
            What are Other Data Types?
        </h3>

        <p>
            Apart from numeric, character, date and time data types,
            SQL Server provides specialized data types for specific
            application requirements.
        </p>

        <p>
            These data types are useful when an application needs to
            store Boolean values, currency, globally unique identifiers,
            binary files, XML documents or other specialized information.
        </p>

    </section>


    <!-- =====================================================
         VISUAL DIAGRAM
         ===================================================== -->

    <section class="mb-5">

        <h3 class="fw-bold mb-4">
            SQL Server Other Data Types
        </h3>

        <div class="row g-3">

            <div class="col-md-6 col-lg-4">

                <div class="border rounded-3 p-4 h-100 bg-light">

                    <h5 class="fw-bold">
                        BIT
                    </h5>

                    <p class="mb-0 text-muted">
                        Stores Boolean values such as 0 and 1.
                    </p>

                </div>

            </div>


            <div class="col-md-6 col-lg-4">

                <div class="border rounded-3 p-4 h-100 bg-light">

                    <h5 class="fw-bold">
                        MONEY
                    </h5>

                    <p class="mb-0 text-muted">
                        Stores monetary values.
                    </p>

                </div>

            </div>


            <div class="col-md-6 col-lg-4">

                <div class="border rounded-3 p-4 h-100 bg-light">

                    <h5 class="fw-bold">
                        UNIQUEIDENTIFIER
                    </h5>

                    <p class="mb-0 text-muted">
                        Stores globally unique identifiers.
                    </p>

                </div>

            </div>


            <div class="col-md-6 col-lg-4">

                <div class="border rounded-3 p-4 h-100 bg-light">

                    <h5 class="fw-bold">
                        BINARY / VARBINARY
                    </h5>

                    <p class="mb-0 text-muted">
                        Stores binary data.
                    </p>

                </div>

            </div>


            <div class="col-md-6 col-lg-4">

                <div class="border rounded-3 p-4 h-100 bg-light">

                    <h5 class="fw-bold">
                        XML
                    </h5>

                    <p class="mb-0 text-muted">
                        Stores XML formatted data.
                    </p>

                </div>

            </div>


            <div class="col-md-6 col-lg-4">

                <div class="border rounded-3 p-4 h-100 bg-light">

                    <h5 class="fw-bold">
                        SQL_VARIANT
                    </h5>

                    <p class="mb-0 text-muted">
                        Stores values of different SQL Server data types.
                    </p>

                </div>

            </div>

        </div>

    </section>


    <!-- =====================================================
         DATA TYPE TABLE
         ===================================================== -->

    <section class="mb-5">

        <h3 class="fw-bold mb-3">
            Common Other Data Types
        </h3>

        <div class="table-responsive">

            <table class="table table-bordered table-striped align-middle">

                <thead class="table-dark">

                    <tr>

                        <th>
                            Data Type
                        </th>

                        <th>
                            Purpose
                        </th>

                        <th>
                            Example
                        </th>

                    </tr>

                </thead>

                <tbody>

                    <tr>

                        <td>
                            <strong>BIT</strong>
                        </td>

                        <td>
                            Stores Boolean or yes/no type values.
                        </td>

                        <td>
                            0 / 1
                        </td>

                    </tr>

                    <tr>

                        <td>
                            <strong>MONEY</strong>
                        </td>

                        <td>
                            Stores monetary values.
                        </td>

                        <td>
                            45000.50
                        </td>

                    </tr>

                    <tr>

                        <td>
                            <strong>SMALLMONEY</strong>
                        </td>

                        <td>
                            Stores smaller-range monetary values.
                        </td>

                        <td>
                            1500.25
                        </td>

                    </tr>

                    <tr>

                        <td>
                            <strong>UNIQUEIDENTIFIER</strong>
                        </td>

                        <td>
                            Stores GUID values.
                        </td>

                        <td>
                            6F9619FF-8B86-D011-B42D-00C04FC964FF
                        </td>

                    </tr>

                    <tr>

                        <td>
                            <strong>BINARY</strong>
                        </td>

                        <td>
                            Stores fixed-length binary data.
                        </td>

                        <td>
                            0x123456
                        </td>

                    </tr>

                    <tr>

                        <td>
                            <strong>VARBINARY</strong>
                        </td>

                        <td>
                            Stores variable-length binary data.
                        </td>

                        <td>
                            0x1234567890
                        </td>

                    </tr>

                    <tr>

                        <td>
                            <strong>XML</strong>
                        </td>

                        <td>
                            Stores XML documents and fragments.
                        </td>

                        <td>
                            &lt;Student&gt;...&lt;/Student&gt;
                        </td>

                    </tr>

                    <tr>

                        <td>
                            <strong>SQL_VARIANT</strong>
                        </td>

                        <td>
                            Stores values of different supported
                            SQL Server data types.
                        </td>

                        <td>
                            100 / 'Hello'
                        </td>

                    </tr>

                </tbody>

            </table>

        </div>

    </section>


    <!-- =====================================================
         BIT
         ===================================================== -->

    <section class="mb-5">

        <h3 class="fw-bold mb-3">
            BIT Data Type
        </h3>

        <p>
            The <strong>BIT</strong> data type is commonly used to store
            Boolean values such as Yes/No, True/False or Active/Inactive.
        </p>

        <div class="code-block mb-3">

            <div class="code-lang-tag">
                SQL
            </div>

            <pre class="mb-0"><code>CREATE TABLE Students
(
    StudentId INT,
    StudentName VARCHAR(100),
    IsActive BIT
);</code></pre>

        </div>

        <p>
            A value of <strong>1</strong> can represent true or active,
            while <strong>0</strong> can represent false or inactive.
        </p>

    </section>


    <!-- =====================================================
         MONEY
         ===================================================== -->

    <section class="mb-5">

        <h3 class="fw-bold mb-3">
            MONEY and SMALLMONEY
        </h3>

        <p>
            The <strong>MONEY</strong> data type is used to store
            monetary values such as salary, fees, price and transaction
            amounts.
        </p>

        <p>
            <strong>SMALLMONEY</strong> is used when a smaller monetary
            range is sufficient.
        </p>

        <div class="code-block mb-3">

            <div class="code-lang-tag">
                SQL
            </div>

            <pre class="mb-0"><code>CREATE TABLE Employees
(
    EmployeeId INT,
    EmployeeName VARCHAR(100),
    Salary MONEY
);</code></pre>

        </div>

    </section>


    <!-- =====================================================
         UNIQUEIDENTIFIER
         ===================================================== -->

    <section class="mb-5">

        <h3 class="fw-bold mb-3">
            UNIQUEIDENTIFIER
        </h3>

        <p>
            The <strong>UNIQUEIDENTIFIER</strong> data type stores a
            globally unique identifier, commonly called a GUID.
        </p>

        <p>
            It is useful when records need identifiers that are unique
            across different systems or databases.
        </p>

        <div class="code-block mb-3">

            <div class="code-lang-tag">
                SQL
            </div>

            <pre class="mb-0"><code>CREATE TABLE Customers
(
    CustomerId UNIQUEIDENTIFIER,
    CustomerName VARCHAR(100)
);

INSERT INTO Customers
(
    CustomerId,
    CustomerName
)
VALUES
(
    NEWID(),
    'Rahul'
);</code></pre>

        </div>

    </section>


    <!-- =====================================================
         BINARY / VARBINARY
         ===================================================== -->

    <section class="mb-5">

        <h3 class="fw-bold mb-3">
            BINARY and VARBINARY
        </h3>

        <p>
            <strong>BINARY</strong> and <strong>VARBINARY</strong> are
            used to store binary data.
        </p>

        <p>
            They can be useful for storing binary information such as
            hashes or other application-specific binary values.
        </p>

        <div class="code-block mb-3">

            <div class="code-lang-tag">
                SQL
            </div>

            <pre class="mb-0"><code>CREATE TABLE Files
(
    FileId INT,
    FileData VARBINARY(MAX)
);</code></pre>

        </div>

    </section>


    <!-- =====================================================
         XML
         ===================================================== -->

    <section class="mb-5">

        <h3 class="fw-bold mb-3">
            XML Data Type
        </h3>

        <p>
            The <strong>XML</strong> data type is used to store XML
            documents and XML fragments.
        </p>

        <div class="code-block mb-3">

            <div class="code-lang-tag">
                SQL
            </div>

            <pre class="mb-0"><code>CREATE TABLE StudentDetails
(
    StudentId INT,
    StudentData XML
);</code></pre>

        </div>

        <p>
            Example XML value:
        </p>

        <div class="code-block">

            <div class="code-lang-tag">
                XML
            </div>

            <pre class="mb-0"><code>&lt;Student&gt;
    &lt;Name&gt;Rahul&lt;/Name&gt;
    &lt;City&gt;Pune&lt;/City&gt;
&lt;/Student&gt;</code></pre>

        </div>

    </section>


    <!-- =====================================================
         SQL_VARIANT
         ===================================================== -->

    <section class="mb-5">

        <h3 class="fw-bold mb-3">
            SQL_VARIANT
        </h3>

        <p>
            The <strong>SQL_VARIANT</strong> data type can store values
            of several supported SQL Server data types.
        </p>

        <p>
            It should be used carefully because it is intended for
            specialized scenarios rather than normal application columns.
        </p>

        <div class="code-block mb-3">

            <div class="code-lang-tag">
                SQL
            </div>

            <pre class="mb-0"><code>CREATE TABLE DynamicValues
(
    Id INT,
    ValueData SQL_VARIANT
);

INSERT INTO DynamicValues
VALUES
(1, 100);

INSERT INTO DynamicValues
VALUES
(2, 'Hello');</code></pre>

        </div>

    </section>


    <!-- =====================================================
         COMPLETE EXAMPLE
         ===================================================== -->

    <section class="mb-5">

        <h3 class="fw-bold mb-3">
            Practical Example
        </h3>

        <p>
            The following example demonstrates several specialized
            data types in a single table.
        </p>

        <div class="code-block mb-3">

            <div class="code-lang-tag">
                SQL
            </div>

            <pre class="mb-0"><code>CREATE TABLE EmployeeDetails
(
    EmployeeId INT,
    EmployeeName VARCHAR(100),
    IsActive BIT,
    Salary MONEY,
    EmployeeGuid UNIQUEIDENTIFIER,
    EmployeeData XML
);</code></pre>

        </div>

    </section>


    <!-- =====================================================
         INSERT EXAMPLE
         ===================================================== -->

    <section class="mb-5">

        <h3 class="fw-bold mb-3">
            Insert Data
        </h3>

        <div class="code-block mb-3">

            <div class="code-lang-tag">
                SQL
            </div>

            <pre class="mb-0"><code>INSERT INTO EmployeeDetails
(
    EmployeeId,
    EmployeeName,
    IsActive,
    Salary,
    EmployeeGuid,
    EmployeeData
)
VALUES
(
    1,
    'Rahul',
    1,
    45000.50,
    NEWID(),
    '&lt;Employee&gt;
        &lt;Department&gt;IT&lt;/Department&gt;
        &lt;City&gt;Pune&lt;/City&gt;
     &lt;/Employee&gt;'
);</code></pre>

        </div>

    </section>


    <!-- =====================================================
         OUTPUT
         ===================================================== -->

    <section class="mb-5">

        <h3 class="fw-bold mb-3">
            Output
        </h3>

        <div class="table-responsive">

            <table class="table table-bordered table-striped align-middle">

                <thead class="table-dark">

                    <tr>
                        <th>EmployeeId</th>
                        <th>EmployeeName</th>
                        <th>IsActive</th>
                        <th>Salary</th>
                        <th>EmployeeGuid</th>
                        <th>EmployeeData</th>
                    </tr>

                </thead>

                <tbody>

                    <tr>

                        <td>1</td>

                        <td>Rahul</td>

                        <td>1</td>

                        <td>45000.50</td>

                        <td>
                            6F9619FF-8B86-D011-B42D-00C04FC964FF
                        </td>

                        <td>
                            &lt;Employee&gt;...&lt;/Employee&gt;
                        </td>

                    </tr>

                </tbody>

            </table>

        </div>

        <p class="mt-3">
            The exact GUID value generated by <strong>NEWID()</strong>
            will be different each time.
        </p>

    </section>


    <!-- =====================================================
         WHEN TO USE
         ===================================================== -->

    <section class="mb-5">

        <h3 class="fw-bold mb-3">
            When Should We Use These Data Types?
        </h3>

        <div class="table-responsive">

            <table class="table table-bordered table-striped">

                <thead class="table-dark">

                    <tr>
                        <th>Requirement</th>
                        <th>Recommended Type</th>
                    </tr>

                </thead>

                <tbody>

                    <tr>
                        <td>True / False or Active / Inactive</td>
                        <td><strong>BIT</strong></td>
                    </tr>

                    <tr>
                        <td>Money or currency values</td>
                        <td><strong>MONEY / SMALLMONEY</strong></td>
                    </tr>

                    <tr>
                        <td>Globally unique identifier</td>
                        <td><strong>UNIQUEIDENTIFIER</strong></td>
                    </tr>

                    <tr>
                        <td>Binary information</td>
                        <td><strong>VARBINARY</strong></td>
                    </tr>

                    <tr>
                        <td>XML documents</td>
                        <td><strong>XML</strong></td>
                    </tr>

                    <tr>
                        <td>Specialized mixed-type values</td>
                        <td><strong>SQL_VARIANT</strong></td>
                    </tr>

                </tbody>

            </table>

        </div>

    </section>


    <!-- =====================================================
         IMPORTANT NOTE
         ===================================================== -->

    <section class="mb-5">

        <div class="alert alert-warning border-0">

            <h5 class="fw-bold">
                Important
            </h5>

            <p class="mb-0">
                Always choose a data type according to the actual
                requirement of the application. Specialized data types
                should be used only when they provide a clear benefit
                for the data being stored.
            </p>

        </div>

    </section>


    <!-- =====================================================
         SUMMARY
         ===================================================== -->

    <section class="mb-4">

        <div class="alert alert-primary border-0">

            <h5 class="fw-bold">
                Summary
            </h5>

            <p class="mb-0">
                In this section, we learned about several specialized
                SQL Server data types including BIT, MONEY, SMALLMONEY,
                UNIQUEIDENTIFIER, BINARY, VARBINARY, XML and SQL_VARIANT.
                We also learned their practical uses and examples.
            </p>

        </div>

    </section>


